<div style="border: 2px solid #1a5276; padding: 15px; text-align: center; background-color: #e0f2f7; margin-bottom: 20px;">
    <h1 style="color: #1a5276; margin: 0;">Lesson Planner – Theme # Shopping at the Market – Lesson # 4</h1>
    <p style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 5px; font-style: italic;">Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</p>
</div>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Lesson #:</b> 4</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Skills Focus:</b> Writing</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Grade:</b> 4th Grade (CEFR: A1.2)</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Scenario:</b> Shopping at the Market</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Theme:</b> I Need Five Yucas.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="2"><b>Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Specific Objective:</b> Writing: Write findings from group research projects for a presentation.</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Outcome:</b> Writing: Can create short texts based on shopping prompts (e.g., 'I need five apples.').
Can write and present short findings from a group project on market items (e.g., 'Apples cost one dollar each.').
Can revise shopping lists or short reports for accuracy by correcting quantities and names (e.g., change 'one orange' to 'two oranges').</p>
        </td>
    </tr>
</table>

<h2 style="color: #1a5276; text-align: center;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>
<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <thead>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f2f2f2; color: #1a5276; width: 33%;">Stage & Description</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f2f2f2; color: #1a5276; width: 34%;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f2f2f2; color: #1a5276; width: 33%;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Engagement, Modeling and Clarification.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> The teacher displays flashcards or realia of market items (pineapple, cassava/yuca, potatoes, apples, bananas). Students choral repeat the names. The teacher then writes the names on the board. Students work in pairs to quickly list 3 items they remember. Example: "Pineapple, yuca, apples."</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> The teacher models writing simple shopping list items on the board. "I need three pineapples. I want five yucas. Potatoes cost two dollars." The teacher emphasizes spelling, capitalization, and punctuation. Teacher highlights pronunciation of /p/ in 'pineapple' and /m/ in 'money' while writing words that contain these sounds (e.g., 'money', 'many', 'pumpkins'). Teacher also models writing numbers 1-10 (e.g., one, two, three) and blends sounds while writing (/w/ /ʌn/ -> one). </p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b>
                    <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0;">
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What do we write first when we want something?" (Expected answer: "I need" or "I want").</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Do we write the number or the word for quantity?" (Expected answer: "The number").</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Can you spell 'yuca'?" (Checks phonemic awareness for spelling).</li>
                    </ul>
                </p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">[Date] <br> 7-10 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 2 — Presentation</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Input of new language/content connected to Scenario: "Shopping at the Market".</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> A short, simple written market report (e.g., "Market News") displayed on a projector or whiteboard. This report contains information about market items, their prices, and common quantities. For example:
                    <br><br>
                    <p style="border: 1px solid #ccc; padding: 10px; background-color: #f9f9f9; text-align: justify;">
                        <b>Market News Today!</b><br>
                        Hello shoppers! Today, yucas are fresh. They cost one dollar each. Many people need five yucas. <br>
                        Pineapples are delicious. One pineapple costs three dollars. <br>
                        Potatoes are cheap. You can buy ten potatoes for two dollars. <br>
                        How much money do you need?
                    </p>
                </p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> Interprets and produces simple written texts related to daily life.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks (for writing readiness):</b> Students read the "Market News" silently.
                    <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0;">
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Teacher asks: "How much does a yuca cost?" (Students write the answer on a mini-whiteboard or notebook: "One dollar.")</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Teacher asks: "What do many people need?" (Students write the answer: "Five yucas.")</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Teacher asks: "How much is one pineapple?" (Students write: "Three dollars.")</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Teacher asks: "Are potatoes cheap or expensive?" (Students write: "Cheap.")</li>
                    </ul>
                </p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">[Date] <br> 10-12 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Accuracy focus on Writing.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b> Students practice writing sentences using WH-Questions ('How much is it?'), Quantities ('I need five potatoes.'), and Present Simple ('I want three apples and one banana.'). Vocabulary: market, price, shopping list, item, cost, pineapple, cassava/yuca, potatoes, buy, need, want, how much, how many, numbers 1-100.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: decimal; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Controlled Practice: Market List Fill-in:</b> The teacher provides a worksheet with a simple shopping list template and incomplete sentences. Students fill in the blanks using numbers and item names.
                        <br>Example:
                        1. I need ____ (5) ____ (yucas).
                        2. How much ____ (is) ____ (one pineapple)?
                        3. I ____ (want) ____ (2) ____ (potatoes).
                        4. Bananas ____ (cost) ____ (one) dollar each.
                        The teacher monitors for correct spelling of items and numbers, and correct grammar.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Semi-controlled Writing: Sentence Builders:</b> The teacher writes sentence frames on the board or provides cards with prompts. Students choose an item and a quantity to complete the sentences in their notebooks.
                        <br>Example Frames:
                        - "I need ______ (number) ______ (item)."
                        - "______ (item) cost ______ (number) dollars."
                        - "How much is the ______ (item)?"
                        Students must write at least three different sentences. E.g., "I need seven potatoes." "Pineapples cost three dollars." "How much is the cassava?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Pair Check & Revision:</b> Students exchange their notebooks with a partner. They check each other's sentences for correct spelling of vocabulary (e.g., 'pineapple', 'money'), correct use of numbers, and sentence structure. They make corrections using a different colored pencil. This reinforces the learning outcome of revising texts for accuracy.</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">[Date] <br> 15-17 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Communicative task where students USE the language in a realistic scenario: "Shopping at the Market".</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Students will work in small groups (3-4 students) to write findings from a simulated "market research project."</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task format:</b> Each group creates a "Market Report" on a large piece of paper or poster board (or in their notebooks) based on items previously discussed or 'researched' (e.g., information from previous lessons about prices and availability). They will write short sentences to describe their findings.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Procedure:</b>
                    <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0;">
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Groups discuss 3-4 market items they want to include in their report (e.g., yucas, pineapples, potatoes, apples).</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">For each item, they write sentences about its price and a common quantity people buy. They can also include adjectives like 'fresh' or 'delicious'.</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Example sentences to guide them:
                            <ul style="list-style-type: circle; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 4px;">
                                <li style="margin-bottom: 2px; text-align: justify;">"Yucas are fresh. They cost one dollar each. We need five yucas."</li>
                                <li style="margin-bottom: 2px; text-align: justify;">"Pineapples are delicious. One pineapple costs three dollars."</li>
                                <li style="margin-bottom: 2px; text-align: justify;">"Potatoes are cheap. You can buy ten potatoes for two dollars."</li>
                            </ul>
                        </li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Groups ensure their report is clearly written, using correct grammar and spelling (paying attention to /p/ and /m/ sounds when writing words like 'pineapple' and 'money', and correct number spelling). They practice reading their report quietly as preparation for a future presentation.</li>
                    </ul>
                </p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">[Date] <br> 10-12 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Formative assessment strategy.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Formative Assessment Strategy:</b> Teacher observation checklist during group work and review of written reports. Peer assessment during the "Pair Check & Revision" activity.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> Each group submits their "Market Report." The teacher checks for individual contributions and overall group output. One student from each group can briefly read a sentence from their report (pre-presentation practice).</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria:</b>
                    <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0;">
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Clarity and legibility of writing.</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Correct use of target vocabulary (market items, price, cost, money).</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Accurate use of grammar (Quantities, Present Simple, WH-questions).</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Correct spelling of words and numbers (1-100).</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Evidence of group collaboration in writing the report.</li>
                    </ul>
                </p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b> Students complete two sentences in their notebooks before leaving:
                    <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0;">
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Today, I learned to write about..."</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"One thing I can write well is..."</li>
                    </ul>
                </p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">[Date] <br> 5 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 6 — Reflection</h3>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student self-reflection prompt:</b>
                    <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0;">
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What part of writing the market report was easy for you?"</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What part of writing the market report was difficult, and how can you practice it more?"</li>
                    </ul>
                </p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher reflection:</b>
                    <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0;">
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What worked well in this writing lesson? (e.g., structured practice, peer feedback, group collaboration).</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What adjustments are needed for future writing tasks or for specific students (e.g., more scaffolding for sentence structure, focused spelling practice on numbers)?</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Did students meet the learning outcome of creating short texts and revising for accuracy?</li>
                    </ul>
                </p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to next lesson:</b> The written market reports from this lesson will serve as the primary content for the "Mediation & Integration" (Lesson 5) project. Students will use these reports to summarize information and prepare a short presentation, integrating their writing and speaking skills. This will also connect to the 21st Century Skills project of presenting findings.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">[Date] <br> 3-4 min</td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>